WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.760
Thundercade, Terrorism has reached new heights!

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:26.060
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:27.800
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.140
And I'm Joe.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:37.820
Guys, what are some things today that are pictured to be as cool as motorcycles were in the 70s and 80s?

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.080
Hmm. Huh.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.300
Wow, I wasn't expecting that.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:43.720
Yeah, that's a tough one.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.000
Give me a second, I'll think of something.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:48.320
Is it just like all future synthwave stuff now, Sean?

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.940
No, no, that's a very niche thing.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.580
Okay. Maybe...

00:00:54.050 --> 00:01:00.320
Teslas? Yeah, Teslas, Cybertrucks, a really high follower count on OKCupid.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.720
Oh, a really high follower count.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.280
That is a good answer. On OKCupid.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:06.460
I'm sorry. I meant to say OnlyFans.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.440
They're the same thing, right?

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.520
Yeah. The end goal is kind of the same.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.360
Intimacy and all that.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:18.500
Yeah. Anyway, that wasn't what this episode was really going to be about.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.740
We're not going to talk about the 80s and today.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:23.200
It's shmup time.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:24.800
That's right, you guys.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:25.940
I know you were waiting.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.600
When were we going to get another shmup on this system?

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.620
We've had a drought.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:30.880
It's time again.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:33.680
Who's excited for some NES shmups?

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.500
I'm excited to take this to new heights.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.200
Yeah, yeah. It kind of sounds like a Roger Ebert review of terrorism.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.600
Oh, the back of the box, right?

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:46.940
Yeah, yeah. Yes, yes.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:56.160
And Joe, you were speaking before the episode that it says reach new heights, but you are a motorcycle on the ground.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.200
Yeah, that's the new height.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.560
The low of the ground.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:01.520
Yeah, low. High is the new low.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.980
You circled too high, so we have to go back to low.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:05.880
Yeah, that's how it works.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:09.040
If you go too high, you end up low, but on another planet now.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.240
So you're playing as a motorcycle.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.020
No, you're playing as a guy riding a motorcycle.

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:15.840
Okay, you know what I mean.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:18.900
You're playing on a motorcycle instead of in a ship.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:23.480
You're playing as the guy's brain controlling the guy on the motorcycle.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:30.940
Yes, yes. But I guess the point I was trying to make is even some of the bosses in this game are just, you know, helicopters or jets themselves,

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.840
and yet they're fighting a motorcycle, which is kind of funny.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.440
And sometimes, like, the boss is just, like, the top of a submarine.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.520
Like, not even, like, a whole submarine.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.500
Just, like, part of it.

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:46.220
So it's even lower.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:47.480
Like, that's underwater.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:51.220
Oh, yeah. That's even newer heights that we can't even fathom.

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:58.260
In Thundercade, you are part of Operation Thundercade.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:08.920
Duh. A special forces operation battling against the nuclear threat of the atomic age terrorist organization of Miracali?

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:10.280
I don't know.

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:13.500
It spells out ADAM, but with two A's.

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:15.020
It kind of looks like a stock ticker.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.700
A-A-T-O-M.

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.400
Too many digits to be a stock ticker.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:26.200
But nevertheless, the atomic age terrorists, I guess they're, you know, they're terrorists in the name,

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.200
which I don't think is, like, that's not really, like, a done thing, right?

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:31.220
No terrorist actually refers to themselves.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.300
I don't think so.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:34.320
Yeah, I think they're usually, like, freedom fighters.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.700
But I appreciate their candor.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.820
Their boldness. Yeah. Self-awareness.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:44.820
They don't give a shit. They want all the superheroes of the world to come up against them and try to take them down on their motorcycle.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:50.360
You play as a guy riding a motorcycle.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:51.980
Sorry if that was unclear earlier.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.780
You're just the guy on the motorcycle.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.160
This isn't Knight Rider.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.520
It's not the talking car.

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:00.120
You play as the guy on the motorcycle.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:05.520
And you can have some, like, sidecar attachments that act as cannons.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:10.520
Or you can have your B-7 bomber, which is, like, out of sight.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:16.740
You can summon him on command if you have the appropriate power-ups to do some damage as well.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:21.480
But otherwise, this is the shmups that we all know, right?

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:29.580
There's not much here to cover in terms of, like, newness or freshness.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.880
The newness thing is the motorcycle, right?

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:40.580
The idea that you're a guy on a motorcycle instead of being a flying spacecraft of any kind.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:44.440
I mean, remember, we've seen other objects, though, B-shmup things.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:47.020
Remember Schoon? Where it's like, now you're a submarine?

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:48.220
That's true.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:53.460
This is not quite as high concept as Schoon.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:57.960
But it at least is getting away from planes and spaceships.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:11.080
Yeah. But, I mean, as far as, like, yeah, the new thing being that you're on this motorcycle is really mostly just something that's, like, a visual and, like, in your own imagination thing.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:15.300
Because otherwise, it plays just like one of those spaceships except for the fact that you can jump.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:21.380
Well, I would say it doesn't quite play exactly like it, but we'll get there.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:25.380
Well, okay, I don't think it plays exactly like it because it's just different.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.600
It's just a different shmup.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:33.440
But I don't think anything about, personally, unless, you know, change my mind, anything about the motorcycle is like, oh, this plays like a motorcycle.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.700
I just think it plays like a slow shmup.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:37.620
It doesn't play like a motorcycle.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.860
Like, it is a cool, like, context for pickups.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.300
Like, oh, it's your sidecar.

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.140
You get a sidecar that can shoot sideways.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:46.680
You get a sidecar that shoots big bullets.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:53.340
But in terms of gameplay, like, a lot of it is just standard shmup fare.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:06:06.160
But the one thing that I think that this game did differently and not quite most of the other games that we're going to compare it to is that, like, cover comes into play.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:14.980
And not saying that it had to just be a motorcycle thing to allow this, but I think it at least had to be ground-based for it to make a lot of sense.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.380
Do you guys agree?

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:24.240
No, that checks out. That is a good point of, like, because that's essentially what I was going to ask is, like, how far does the motorcycle gimmick get them?

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:37.560
But you're right. The idea of it being on ground matters because in all of our NES space games, we just assume that everybody is at the exact XYZ coordinates that, like, every attack would hit, you know?

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:48.620
But in this game, because you're on the ground and because your cover is also something that is destroyable so that you can get power-ups and stuff like that, that's how you find those things.

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:54.080
There is a game system there of, like, take out the enemies first.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:07:00.560
Then, I guess, if you still have time while the stage is scrolling, then take out your barriers to see if you can uncover some power-ups.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.580
There is a game-y aspect to that.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:03.940
Yeah. Yeah, you know what?

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:07.640
I'll be honest. I sort of took for granted the fact that you can take cover.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:14.160
Like, I guess it's been a while since we played a shmup, so it didn't stand out to me as something new or something that we don't see very often.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.100
But, yeah, I hadn't really thought of that.

00:07:16.180 --> 00:07:18.340
That is something that's a little different.

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:24.680
Well, also, you know, the idea that the power-ups are just something you pick up is a little different than most shmups.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.780
I know this isn't the first time that's been done.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:38.880
But it is a different sense of progression where you're never too far away from being the most powered-up thing because you just have to find, you know, the power-ups through your destructibles.

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:42.460
So this way you can reattach them or become even stronger.

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:52.240
Some games we've seen, like, it requires points or it requires, like, the conscious selection to not choose a power-up now to get a better power-up later.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:55.120
In this one, it's just available to you.

00:07:55.180 --> 00:08:04.020
And if you can reach it, which sometimes is an obstacle in itself, going into the line of fire to reach those power-ups, if you can reach them, now you have them.

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:09.840
But if you lose them, it's also easy to kind of gain them back.

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:23.980
Yeah. Because there's also – it's one of those situations – I can't quite remember the last time we've seen this in a shmup – but where you can have two sidecars at a time.

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:33.220
But once you pick up another power-up, and this power-up may or may not be more powerful, you could also get a power-up that sort of downgrades you.

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:34.520
You do have to avoid those.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:46.540
So that – you also just want to be kind of choosy once you're in a place that you're comfortable in or a specific power-up that, like, suits the terrain that you're playing in.

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:53.180
Like, sometimes you'll want those side-shooting sidecars, and sometimes you really don't need them at all.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:23.160
Yeah.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:26.880
You end up being back to being not powerful or dead pretty quickly.

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:39.740
And that only really becomes a problem during boss fights because, for the most part, I kind of like that, yeah, it's high stakes and you will lose these things pretty fast just because of how many enemies and bullets are being thrown at you.

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:43.520
But you can always pick them up very quickly, again, through the regular stage.

00:09:43.660 --> 00:09:52.240
So it's not – it doesn't run into that gradius problem where you won't have the ability to, like, recover all your power-ups if you have to start a stage over.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:10:05.580
You know, like, they're always kind of, you know, within reach except for when you get to the point in the stages where it stops scrolling and now you have boss fights where no additional power-ups will come your way.

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:16.620
I'm kind of a little shocked that they didn't choose to, like, make some disposable barriers since that seems to be part of the gameplay here into the boss fights.

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:28.380
But to me, that is where it actually falls apart because of how easily bullets take out your power-ups and how quickly you reapply them.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:41.900
It's a little strange that once you get to the actual, like, meat and potatoes of the shmup, the boss fight, which is a very long one-on-one fight, that you're just kind of expected to duke it out with whatever you came into the fight with.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:50.080
Yeah, and that – I mean, that's – this isn't – this isn't unique to this game, like, especially with something like Gradius.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:11:04.560
But, no, it's really frustrating to end up, like, in a boss fight with just this peashooter that you start out with on your lone motorcycle with no sidecars.

00:11:04.740 --> 00:11:12.080
And I think when you die, you – like, lives, you just respawn in the same screen.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:13.800
Immediately, yeah.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:22.880
So you have to use a continue if you don't have the firepower or you don't have the skill to use your current firepower, which is really frustrating.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:36.960
And there's no tell either, you know, in enemies or in boss fights to know if you're actually, like, doing any damage, which, granted, is fine for most of the enemies because most enemies are one or three hits max if you're, like, a tank or something.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:42.800
It is a little weird that there's no – for things that have extra health, there's no, like, sign of damage.

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:44.260
And I'm not talking about, like, cosmetically.

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:45.940
I'm just talking about blinking, you know.

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:53.840
But it's really bad in boss fights because I don't know about you guys, but even the first one, Sean, you mentioned that submarine half-submerged.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:12:08.660
Yeah. It has no – you would think maybe there's, like, a weak spot that I'm not hitting because otherwise it's just absorbing your bullets and there's no health bar forwarded or anything like that.

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:11.780
And these guys are kind of damaged sponges.

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:16.540
Like, they have a lot of health to them, mini boss or full boss.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:27.700
And so I feel like, you know, there needed to be some kind of communication in terms of, like, what am I – you know, how far along am I or am I doing any damage to these?

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:39.460
Because I felt like with that first stage boss fight with the plane, I was, like, actually shocked at, like, a shmup starting off like this after having, like, mostly easy enemies.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:48.480
Just a plane that just shoots bullets like crazy, expects you to just, like, dodge everything but last long enough to take it down.

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:50.100
And I did make it through this stage.

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.140
It's not impossible.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:13:01.220
But it is just surprising how all of a sudden this thing becomes, like, so – like, a bullet hell but where there's very little in your corner.

00:13:01.340 --> 00:13:02.600
There's very little going for you.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:10.700
And for me, like, first of all, I do think this game is hard even when you're just in the standard levels.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:23.580
But the thing that really peeves me in this game is that, like, in these bosses, like, these plane bosses, it sort of forgets that you're ground – that you're, like, a ground-based – you're a motorcycle.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:32.280
All of a sudden, this plane just starts moving any which way and acts like you're in a flying shmup.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:34.460
And I just thought that that was silly.

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:37.620
And I don't know if you guys felt that as well.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:50.240
But if you're going to, like, have the context of your game be that this is, like, all happening on the ground, like, maybe a plane that moves in all eight directions shouldn't be a boss.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.380
Well, even you.

00:13:52.580 --> 00:13:54.120
Even the motorcycle moves.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:56.440
You know, you could just move directly sideways.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:14:07.360
Yeah, that's true. And, like, that's kind of what I was referencing at the beginning where I was like, nothing about it being a motorcycle really feels like it's different than the ship other than what you mentioned, the ground cover.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:21.920
And in, like, the – but at least, like, in the standard levels, like, the screen is moving – not fast, but it's moving enough that it's like, oh, this is just, like, me turning and the camera is following the motorcycle.

00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:24.440
But in the bosses, it just doesn't make any goddamn sense.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:27.140
So, yeah, that's, I guess, what I was saying.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:30.440
Yeah, I ended up, for most of the bosses, just trying to save my airstrikes.

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:34.620
And then I would just call in, like, three or four airstrikes at once and just destroy them.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:38.020
But, yeah, I mean, it wasn't particularly fun to do it that way.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.060
It was just the most viable way.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:46.300
And the airstrike is a very satisfying kind of power-up, one that feels very strong.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:49.480
I don't know how strong it actually is or whatever because I only used it on boss fights.

00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:57.100
But I wouldn't be opposed to seeing more ridiculous power-ups like that in shmups.

00:14:57.260 --> 00:15:05.060
You know, we saw, like, in 1942, you just have, like – you know, you do an aerial dodge as your secondary button.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:08.600
And that's not really, like, that cool of a thing to do.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:10.080
That's just, like, a flight maneuver.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:20.040
However, calling on your own B-17 bomber to then, like, you know, just do a raid on the boss is just really cool.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:23.420
It feels like something – like, you know how, like, in Call of Duty when you get those killstreaks.

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:24.780
You get those airstrikes, yeah.

00:15:25.060 --> 00:15:27.760
Yeah, you're just able to, like, have insane power-ups.

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.320
That's what that feels like.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:36.660
But in a shmup, I wouldn't – you know, for a game like Thundercade, I wouldn't mind being able to summon a thunderstorm that just takes out the entire screen.

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:38.540
Or summon Bahamut Zero.

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:39.980
Right. Yeah.

00:15:39.980 --> 00:15:42.540
Or cast Zetaflare. Or Donald Duck.

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:50.860
Yeah. I can confirm, though, that when you're really feeling trapped or cornered or there's a lot of enemies on the screen,

00:15:51.440 --> 00:15:55.820
one of those, you know, one of those airstrikes will take out a significant chunk of every enemy.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:59.320
It does pack a big punch for those situations.

00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:06.860
So, kind of, you know, it was kind of – I had to decide whether I wanted to save them for the bosses, which I ultimately did,

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:10.940
or use them in those very cool moments when, you know, when I could clear part of the screen.

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:20.120
Not to, like, harp on – I mean, because we've done this in other shmup games as well.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:27.680
But, like, you know, the amount of bullets that are coming at you on this screen – and the speeds of the bullets vary, too.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.280
Like, the size of the bullets vary, for that matter.

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:33.920
This was a little too much for me personally.

00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:35.500
I had my limit.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.960
I agree. With this game.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:42.380
And that's why I thought that this game was much more difficult than a lot of the ones we played.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:48.940
Really? See, I thought that what bothered me about this was not the difficulty, but it was the slowness of it.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:57.000
Like, I never felt like – maybe it was because I used the plane a little bit, but, like, I never felt like I was, like, overwhelmed by bullets.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:59.820
I just felt like I was, like, just trudging along.

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:02.840
And, like, that's what my problem was.

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:08.340
Like, I never felt like it was super bullet hell-ish compared to a lot of other shmups we played where everything's really fast.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:13.700
Like, I feel like most shmups I don't like because I'm just particularly bad at shmups and I have slow reaction time.

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:20.620
This one I felt – I mean, I still wasn't good at it, but I felt like it was more manageable but just never got exciting.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:31.440
I think a part of it for me is, like, the bane of my existence was the helicopters because they just come in and they're moving fast and their bullets are moving fast.

00:17:31.580 --> 00:17:33.800
And sometimes they just blend into the background.

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:38.580
And so if I have a sidecar, I'm losing it there.

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:41.320
And if I don't, I'm dying there.

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:47.800
It was just, like, whenever you got those, like, little helicopter raids on you, that would just ruin me.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:49.860
Yeah, yeah, I hear that.

00:17:49.860 --> 00:17:58.160
And also, full disclosure, when I'm talking about it being not – you know, never getting super bullet hell-y, I'm only talking about, like, the first maybe two and a half levels.

00:17:58.260 --> 00:17:59.640
I didn't get very far in this game.

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:02.080
So maybe it does get worse as it goes on.

00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:09.660
Well, I think a bigger problem is, like, for the regular stage, right, you can just knock out the enemies that are shooting at you and they're gone.

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:15.200
On the boss fights, it's all or nothing in terms of fighting these bosses.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:20.300
I would have appreciated if even, like – you know, and we've seen this in games like Contra.

00:18:20.480 --> 00:18:35.460
It doesn't have to be exclusive to shmups where if you're taking on a plane, right, already ridiculous as it is, you should be able to take off the individual cannons so that it slowly becomes a maybe, like, easier fight because it's so hard right at the get-go.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:47.860
But instead, it just becomes one of these things where even if you learn the pattern of, like, okay, the bullets are in a spray formation where they make, like, wide Vs and then small Vs on the way out.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:49.220
Like, who cares, right?

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:51.200
Like, first off, that sounds like nonsense to me.

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:55.900
But, like, let's pretend that I was good at something like that where I could recognize that pattern.

00:18:56.180 --> 00:18:57.760
You have to do it for so long.

00:18:57.760 --> 00:19:02.440
There's never a moment where you feel like you're gaining leverage on these things until they blow up.

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:05.000
Yeah, exactly.

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:18.040
Because I do think that some of them at least, like, they will stop shooting from the ports that you – because a lot of them are, like, multi-stage, like, enemies.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:22.100
Like, at least, like, if you blow up a turret, it'll stop shooting out of that turret.

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:26.000
But I feel like it just keeps getting faster on the turrets that you haven't blown up.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.620
So it ends up being, like, a net zero sort of thing.

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:34.100
Maybe that was just how I experienced it in my mind.

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:57.000
So just to talk a little more about the overall speed of it, I mean, did it bother anyone else that it was, like, so trudgingly slow?

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:05.020
I feel like – I guess, obviously, if you're being literal about it, being on a motorcycle is technically slower than being on a spaceship.

00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:08.500
But you're supposed to feel fast on a motorcycle.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:12.660
It's almost like this goes deliberately at, like, a crawling speed.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.940
And it does not feel like a motorcycle to me.

00:20:16.000 --> 00:20:18.640
It just feels – it feels like a trudge.

00:20:18.640 --> 00:20:25.480
I know what you're saying, but even the feeling of going backwards on a motorcycle just feels wrong.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:41.100
Like, movement here in terms of speed, the scroll is slow in itself, but also just, like, the way that the motorcycle moves has no sense of speed itself regardless of the scrolling the limit.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:43.900
They kind of, like, messed up on two fronts.

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:53.160
Like, in order to make it feel like there's some speed, like, you can have the enemies move relatively to you at the same pace, I think.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:59.440
But then you have to, like, recontextualize the backgrounds as moving, like, constantly.

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:07.500
Like, in a space shmup, which is a lot easier because all you need is, like, a star field being animated as moving.

00:21:07.860 --> 00:21:14.300
Whereas in this, like, they want you to use the buildings as cover so you can't have the buildings move past you fast.

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:28.400
And then at the end, like, when you're fighting, you know, the end boss, the dreaded nuclear reactor, like, you're literally just sitting in a room, but you're just swerving back and forth and somehow that makes you move.

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:30.380
Yeah, it doesn't make a lot of sense.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:35.900
Yeah, yeah. And, you know, it's like – I know that this would totally change the game and I'm not suggesting that they would do this.

00:21:35.900 --> 00:21:39.740
But, you know, we just recently played, and I'm blanking, the motorboat –

00:21:41.180 --> 00:21:46.480
Cobra Triangle. Like, that made you feel like you're in a boat.

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:50.180
And, yes, if you were to go too far in that direction with this, it would be a totally different game.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:51.900
I'm not suggesting that.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:22:00.920
But, like, they could go somewhat in that direction and just make the physics and the way you turn feel a little more like a motorcycle.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:05.160
And I'm not even saying that because I really want a game that feels like a motorcycle.

00:22:05.400 --> 00:22:11.300
I just – like, I'm not sure we fully sold, if you guys agree with me, just how dull this game is.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:12.820
Like, I feel like it's just really poor.

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:14.420
Yeah, we're kind of overhyping it, I think.

00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:24.820
Well, okay, we're not overhyping it because I would say I even went as far as earlier this week on our Twitter page to just take a random still from the gameplay.

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:30.920
And I said, out of context, if you know nothing about this game, this looks like a glitched page.

00:22:31.300 --> 00:22:37.900
Like, it looks like the motorcycle is in the water and then there's an area with more water inside that water.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:38.940
This is the blue level.

00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:41.720
Oh, with all the hills that don't look like hills.

00:22:41.720 --> 00:22:43.900
It just looks like nonsense.

00:22:44.440 --> 00:22:46.200
Yeah. It looks like a nonsense sprite sheet.

00:22:46.360 --> 00:22:49.140
Yeah. And meanwhile, that's just like a still from the game.

00:22:49.660 --> 00:22:51.100
It's not a pretty game.

00:22:51.100 --> 00:22:57.980
It's not – you know, I didn't want to play our whole hand before the Essential games.

00:22:58.180 --> 00:23:00.080
No, I'm just giving it all up right now.

00:23:00.100 --> 00:23:01.580
I'm telling you. I'm not voting this Essential.

00:23:03.040 --> 00:23:04.600
But, like, you know what?

00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:05.960
I know what you mean, Joe.

00:23:07.380 --> 00:23:11.300
But I also don't think that it's the worst game that we played.

00:23:11.300 --> 00:23:14.440
And we have to cover, like, you know, all the different aspects of it too.

00:23:14.440 --> 00:23:23.760
But if you would like to say more, other than just the slowness of the speed of other pet peeves that bothered you about this game, I will listen.

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:30.820
Well, here, first of all, you started the conversation right now that I think at least – what are there, six stages?

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:37.780
I think at least three, at least three of the six stages look, you know, texture-wise just look like a total mess.

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:39.280
Like, that was the first thing that I thought of too.

00:23:39.400 --> 00:23:42.720
I was like, what? Why are they – look, I get that they're trying to go for, like, a textured ground.

00:23:42.720 --> 00:23:48.500
I'd say the one that stands out the most to me is the tunnel.

00:23:48.740 --> 00:23:52.360
Because, like, you're going through, yeah, all of these places.

00:23:52.580 --> 00:23:55.340
Like, maybe they don't, like, pass themselves off as a city.

00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:58.400
And they don't really pass themselves off as, like, a military base.

00:23:58.420 --> 00:24:02.880
But at least, like, the ground looks like it's ground or a road or something.

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:06.940
And then you get in the tunnel and then you're just playing on, like, a white field.

00:24:07.060 --> 00:24:11.780
And things are popping out from, like, nowhere or from the sides.

00:24:11.780 --> 00:24:14.800
And – but there's, like – it doesn't look like it's rocky.

00:24:15.120 --> 00:24:18.660
It doesn't look like it's a tunnel that's paved.

00:24:18.660 --> 00:24:21.280
It just looks like they forgot to texture this.

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:25.380
Yeah. It's weird because of how much over-textured other levels are.

00:24:25.480 --> 00:24:27.400
And this one has literally no texture.

00:24:27.620 --> 00:24:33.880
And, like, you see a pothole that, like, when you blow something up and it just looks like something that's, like, floating down through space.

00:24:33.880 --> 00:24:37.480
Because suddenly there's, like, a little piece of texture.

00:24:39.300 --> 00:24:44.140
And another thing – this is, you know, maybe getting into a little more nitpicky.

00:24:44.340 --> 00:24:55.400
But why is there just one song that does not sound like it fits this – it sounds like it's, like, the – it sounds like a song that goes at the end of, like, a coming-of-age movie.

00:24:56.320 --> 00:24:59.260
Like, it's a very, like, happy – like, oh, like, we're doing it.

00:24:59.320 --> 00:25:00.200
Like, we're doing it now.

00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:01.140
Like, it's not exciting.

00:25:01.140 --> 00:25:02.320
It's not action-y.

00:25:02.320 --> 00:25:06.240
It's like, oh, I turned my life around is what the vibe I get from this music.

00:25:06.640 --> 00:25:10.800
Well, you're trying to turn your life around from terrorism.

00:25:11.360 --> 00:25:12.280
That's true. To new heights.

00:25:12.680 --> 00:25:22.340
That is true. Well, there is a questionable ending to the game, right, where you show up at this nuclear plant that I believe belongs to the terrorist organization, Atom.

00:25:23.740 --> 00:25:27.580
And they are, like, just a bunch of soldiers in a bunker.

00:25:27.640 --> 00:25:30.080
So it's not even, like, a final boss where, like –

00:25:30.080 --> 00:25:31.400
In the nuclear reactor.

00:25:31.400 --> 00:25:34.600
Yeah, they're just in the nuclear reactor, and you're shooting at them.

00:25:34.800 --> 00:25:40.320
Somehow you're, like, shooting at the guys all the way at the top of the reactor, too, even though you're on a motorcycle.

00:25:40.760 --> 00:25:50.880
You take them all out, and then you proceed to blow up the nuclear reactor, causing what I can only imagine is, you know, atomic levels of bad.

00:25:51.040 --> 00:25:52.340
Yeah, catastrophic danger.

00:25:52.520 --> 00:25:55.800
Which makes me wonder, were they really the terrorists?

00:25:56.040 --> 00:25:57.240
Or were these guys just caught on guard?

00:25:57.240 --> 00:25:59.280
It sounds like, yeah, you're the terrorist here.

00:25:59.280 --> 00:26:01.740
Yeah, like, they're hiding – they're doing the last thing.

00:26:01.840 --> 00:26:08.340
The last resort is that the only soldiers left are now, like, trying to do a shootout with you in the bunkers.

00:26:08.600 --> 00:26:10.960
I mean, Chernobyl had only occurred not that long ago.

00:26:10.960 --> 00:26:15.220
I wouldn't say that it's the best idea to blow up a nuclear reactor.

00:26:15.520 --> 00:26:19.260
You know, didn't they see the HBO miniseries?

00:26:19.340 --> 00:26:25.140
I don't know. Would you be surprised to know that there are not one sequel and spinoff for this game?

00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:29.020
Absolutely not. And since there are no sequels and spinoffs, there's only one thing left to do.

00:26:29.160 --> 00:26:31.180
That is the Essential Games list.

00:26:34.140 --> 00:26:35.360
Sean, we're going to start with you.

00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:51.400
There exists a combination of game mechanics and decisions that make a motorcycle-based shmup work.

00:26:52.100 --> 00:26:55.300
But this is not quite that combination.

00:26:56.040 --> 00:27:02.220
I do appreciate that they tried some things, but they didn't do it very well at all.

00:27:02.300 --> 00:27:03.700
So this is not essential.

00:27:04.660 --> 00:27:11.380
Joe? Yeah, so I know everyone's on the edge of their seat about what my vote's going to be, but here goes.

00:27:12.260 --> 00:27:21.560
Yeah, I do think that, yeah, this is like, there are a couple of elements that are interesting elements that they put into a bad game.

00:27:21.800 --> 00:27:26.420
Like, I think that that's, like, you know, I never like shmups.

00:27:26.420 --> 00:27:27.660
I rarely like shmups.

00:27:27.900 --> 00:27:33.560
But this one is not, like, a dislike just because shmups aren't my thing.

00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:35.600
This one just felt really boring to me.

00:27:35.700 --> 00:27:38.280
So I'm going to not vote it essential.

00:27:39.480 --> 00:27:40.680
That's very surprising.

00:27:41.060 --> 00:27:42.400
Yes. I'm surprised.

00:27:42.400 --> 00:27:50.280
I would say that for those of you looking for a game where you're on a motorcycle and you shoot bullets, look no further than Mach Rider.

00:27:50.360 --> 00:27:51.980
Mach Rider? Did you call me?

00:27:52.140 --> 00:27:53.760
That is how you do it, baby.

00:27:54.300 --> 00:27:56.800
So maybe three of the quickest no's we've ever had on the show.

00:27:56.800 --> 00:28:01.160
But I really, I don't think this is, like, yes, it is in the bottom half for sure.

00:28:01.340 --> 00:28:02.860
But I don't think it's the worst game.

00:28:02.860 --> 00:28:05.380
I just don't think it's ever worth talking about again.

00:28:05.580 --> 00:28:13.440
And so we will only reference it as a joke in future episodes, like when we refer to Street Cop for two episodes in a row.

00:28:14.300 --> 00:28:15.180
I can't wait.

00:28:15.180 --> 00:28:16.620
These are the things that happen sometimes.

00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:21.940
Sean, any other episodes you want to call out right now as just truly terrible?

00:28:23.100 --> 00:28:25.740
That the episode was terrible or the game was terrible?

00:28:25.740 --> 00:28:29.200
I would love to hear what episodes you think are terrible.

00:28:29.420 --> 00:28:30.960
But, yeah, let's stick to games right now.

00:28:32.060 --> 00:28:36.100
You know, I don't really know.

00:28:36.460 --> 00:28:39.560
I mean, it's hard when you put me on the spot like that.

00:28:39.660 --> 00:28:41.780
I think all games are great.

00:28:42.160 --> 00:28:46.160
Every game is perfect in its own little way.

00:28:46.460 --> 00:28:49.620
There's no such thing as a free lunch.

00:28:50.480 --> 00:28:51.460
There you go.

00:28:51.720 --> 00:28:53.300
Joe, any other thoughts?

00:28:53.980 --> 00:28:55.160
Any other thoughts?

00:28:55.160 --> 00:29:03.820
You know, I'll say that this game recommends for a safety precaution that you pause it for 10 to 15 minutes after two hours of more.

00:29:04.040 --> 00:29:07.740
Not for your safety, but because it extends the life of the game pack.

00:29:08.200 --> 00:29:09.400
I never knew that.

00:29:09.540 --> 00:29:11.280
But that's what it says in the manual.

00:29:11.740 --> 00:29:14.120
It might not be true, but it says that in the manual.

00:29:14.700 --> 00:29:16.260
Well, I appreciate that tip.

00:29:17.920 --> 00:29:22.260
Maybe certain copies of Thundercade are worth more because they have less miles on them.

00:29:22.480 --> 00:29:23.600
Right. Yeah. That's true.

00:29:23.680 --> 00:29:25.060
What's the blue book on this game?

00:29:25.360 --> 00:29:31.840
Right. You know, actually, I did look at that, and it's a rather cheap game as long as you're not looking for the box.

00:29:31.840 --> 00:29:33.060
Like most NES games.

00:29:33.200 --> 00:29:35.340
For some reason, all of a sudden, the boxes are very hot.

00:29:35.600 --> 00:29:37.500
You have a box, not even the game.

00:29:38.080 --> 00:29:39.320
Just sell that thing right now.

00:29:39.560 --> 00:29:44.220
Don't buy the game and then sell them together because most of the cost goes to the game.

00:29:44.380 --> 00:29:48.560
Yet another example of nostalgia price fixing.

00:29:49.260 --> 00:29:50.320
Yeah. We're doing it all day.

00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:51.460
Also, you know what I was just thinking?

00:29:51.460 --> 00:29:55.380
Since you were put on the spot about episodes and stuff like that, Dr.

00:29:55.560 --> 00:29:56.780
Jekyll and Mr. Hyde.

00:29:56.900 --> 00:29:59.140
Oh, yeah. From episode 174.

00:29:59.480 --> 00:30:03.540
Now, that is a game that people talk about all the time and shit on.

00:30:03.680 --> 00:30:05.120
And yet, I think Dr.

00:30:05.220 --> 00:30:07.640
Jekyll and Mr. Hyde is a better game than Thundercade.

00:30:07.940 --> 00:30:09.320
Well, the thing about Dr.

00:30:09.460 --> 00:30:13.400
Jekyll and Mr. Hyde is that it's more unique than bad.

00:30:13.540 --> 00:30:16.300
Like, bad and unique, you'll live on forever.

00:30:16.860 --> 00:30:22.020
Bad and whatever this is, nostalgia will never talk about you again.

00:30:22.440 --> 00:30:24.600
And that's really it for this episode.

00:30:24.600 --> 00:30:30.140
We will certainly be talking to you again next Friday when we do The Adventures of Tom Sawyer.

00:30:30.480 --> 00:30:32.120
We'll do a reading of it, I suppose.

00:30:32.520 --> 00:30:36.420
Yeah, yeah. I guess we'll play the game too, but might as well read an excerpt from the book.

00:30:36.960 --> 00:30:39.000
Wasn't expecting this to be a video game.

00:30:39.120 --> 00:30:40.440
It's made by Winky Soft.

00:30:40.660 --> 00:30:41.500
Winky Soft?

00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:43.080
Winky Soft.

00:30:43.180 --> 00:30:48.200
Ugh. I guess I shouldn't have said, like, soft because it's like software, so it's Winky Soft.

00:30:49.460 --> 00:30:50.340
Winky Soft.

00:30:51.960 --> 00:30:54.180
Whoa, whoa, whoa. I didn't say nothing.

00:30:54.600 --> 00:30:58.060
Eh, it's like a PG-13, mostly R-rated podcast anyway.

